", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Nellie Pou (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Rep. Nellie Pou seeks re-election in a northern New Jersey district that Donald Trump carried, one of the few Trump-won seats Democrats hold. She faces Republican Rosemary Pino, a first-time candidate who won her primary but has struggled financially, along with independent Terrisa Bukovinac. Pou has heavily out-raised her opponent and holds a large cash advantage, with no outside spending reported on either side.\n\nNo public polls cover the race, but every major rating service places it in the Safe or Likely Democratic column, and prediction markets give Pou roughly a 97 percent chance of winning. Local outlets have endorsed her, while Republican efforts to frame the race around Trump's gains here have been complicated by deportation politics in a heavily Hispanic district. The fundamentals point to a comfortable Democratic hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9625, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9596, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9671, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9566, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9611, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9669, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9744, "margin": 13.4}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9657, "margin": 12.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9546, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9588, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9626, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9636, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-0